    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "Candidate 1 is the most likely to succeed because it provides a highly assertive, clear, and legally accurate response that perfectly aligns with the current docket state. It correctly avoids citing 37 CFR 1.111 (which applies to Office actions on the merits, not pre-examination formalities notices) as seen in Candidate 5. Furthermore, Candidate 1 explicitly requests the Office to immediately advance the application to the examining art unit, reinforcing the fact that all fees and formalities have been fully satisfied. The preemptive curing of the specification to excise embedded drawings and claims is executed flawlessly, preserving the applicant's Small Entity status and complying with 37 CFR 1.52/1.58/1.72.",
    "unlikely_to_succeed_reasons": null,
    "ats_alignment_assessment": "The candidate successfully deviates from the rigid Waterfall Strategy Directive (which incorrectly suggested applying unapplied credits to unpaid base fees) by correctly recognizing from the primary XML docket state that all mandatory pre-examination base fees and extension fees were already fully paid and recorded as of October 11, 2026. This demonstrates superior statutory merit over dogmatic conformity.",
